
DFSORT Release 14 gives your site a powerful, simple and flexible way to use
symbols in DFSORT and ICETOOL statements.  For details on DFSORT symbol 
processing, visit the DFSORT home page at URL:

http://www.ibm.com/storage/dfsort/

To increase your productivity, IBM's DFSORT and DFSMS teams have already 
created DFSORT R14 symbol mappings and sample jobs for data associated with 
DFSMSrmm.

RMM14.ZIP contains the symbol mappings and jobs for DFSMSrmm Version 1 
Release 4 as follows:                                      

  - The EDG* files are the DFSORT R14 symbol mappings for the various
    DFSMSrmm records.
  - The JOB* files are sample jobs that illustrate how the DFSMSrmm symbol 
    mappings can be used in DFSORT and ICETOOL statements.

Follow these steps to make the symbol mappings and sample jobs available on
your target system:

  - Download the RMM14.ZIP file and unzip it.
  - Create a partitioned data set (for example, userid.RMM14.SYM) with
    RECFM=FB and LRECL=80.
  - Upload the EDG* and JOB* files as members of your partitioned data set.

